description:
You are a studio manager gathering technical specifications for a new microphone locker. Research three industry-standard microphones: Shure SM7B, Neumann U 87 Ai, and Audio-Technica AT2020.

For each microphone:
1. Navigate to the official manufacturer's website (shure.com, neumann.com, audio-technica.com).
2. Locate the product page and download the official Data Sheet or User Guide (PDF) to '~/Downloads/'.
3. Bookmark the product page in a new Firefox bookmark folder named 'Studio Tech Specs'.
4. Extract the 'Output Impedance' (in Ohms) and 'Sensitivity' (at 1kHz).

Create a JSON file at '~/Documents/mic_specs.json' with the following structure (replace values with your findings):

{
  "shure_sm7b": {
    "manufacturer_url": "...",
    "impedance_ohms": 150,
    "sensitivity_dbv_pa": -59.0
  },
  "neumann_u87ai": {
    "manufacturer_url": "...",
    "impedance_ohms": 200,
    "sensitivity_mv_pa": 28.0
  },
  "at2020": {
    "manufacturer_url": "...",
    "impedance_ohms": 100,
    "sensitivity_dbv_pa": -37.0
  }
}

Note: Pay attention to units. Neumann typically reports sensitivity in mV/Pa, while others often use dBV/Pa.
